{"t": 1794116163.7386937, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*[AG-7731] PaymentGatewayErrors checkout \u2014 root cause found, fix pushed*\n\n*Symptom:* Gateway 4xx rate 38% for checkout since 07:41 UTC (all charges rejected).\n\n*Root cause:* checkout/gateway.py built the charge payload with the amount in major units (e.g. `12.34`). The gateway API was switched to 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\"), which requires `amount` as an integer in minor units. Every charge now fails with `400 invalid_amount: \"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34\"` \u2014 visible in Loki `{app=\"checkout\"}`.\n\n*Fix:* `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents using Decimal with ROUND_HALF_UP (12.34 -> 1234) and keeps `currency: EUR`. No other fields/endpoints changed.\n\n*Impact:* 100% of new charges were being rejected while the gateway stayed on the new API version. After deploy, confirm the 4xx rate returns to baseline and watch the first few charges in Loki/Sentry."}, "ok": true}
